From 431773cbb31d4691b50b2f7f7d1f0d96c77132ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:12:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PM P0: measured baseline + plan (docs/plans/PM_PLAN.md)

Opens audit candidate #3 after XHCI and MSI closed.  Baseline,
measured 2026-10-21: the kernel lane fabricates only
RSDP/RSDT/XSDT/MADT -- there is no FADT and no DSDT anywhere, so PM
is undiscoverable from ACPI except through SeaBIOS' own tables.
The G5 PM block models exactly one register (24-bit PM Timer at
PMBASE+8, deterministic from vtime); PM1_STS/EN read 0, PM1_CNT
sleep writes are swallowed, which means an ACPI power-off from a
SeaBIOS-lane guest hangs after "Power down" today.  Nobody drives
SCI (IRQ 9 is free).  The north star consumes no PM (its ACPI use
is MADT enumeration for SMP), like it consumes no MSI: the audience
is other guests and surface honesty.  The machine does have the
S5 endpoint ready-made (stop_requested, currently debugger-only)
and reset (0xCF9).

Ledger D1-D5 maps to P1 (PM1 registers, SCI, S5), P2 (FADT +
minimal DSDT _S5 + GPE0), P3 (S1).  Decisions: sleep types are
table-driven and the P2 DSDT publishes exactly what P1 decodes;
SCI is a level on IRQ 9 by the fleet convention; TMR_STS latches
on the true 24-bit overflow in pm_advance; SMI_CMD stays 0 (no
fabricated SMM); the S1 fork (real parking vs zero-duration wake)
is recorded for a P2 measurement.  Docs only, no behaviour change.
